Splash (https://github.com/incoai/splash)

The full Apache-2.0 license is reproduced in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/splash_moe/LICENSE.

The grouped GGUF MoE kernels and host plan in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/splash_moe/{abi.h,moe.metal} and
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_splash_moe.cpp are adapted from Splash revision
1482f6bbc2abf12375332725302019594150b6cb, runtime/ops/MoE.cpp,
runtime/metal/abi/MoE.h, runtime/metal/kernels/shared/{moe,moe_gguf}.metal
and runtime/metal/kernels/common/{moe_expert_slab,gguf_column_tile,
gguf_staged_tile}.h. They preserve GPU expert grouping, dynamic row tiers,
the sparse column tile, shared expert scheduling and fused gate/up, with
decoding adapted to mlx-node's three-array quantized storage.

The optional register-based M8 expert path in the same files follows
runtime/metal/kernels/decode/linear_gguf_sgmatrix.metal and the expert
schedule in runtime/ops/MoE.hpp at the same revision. It prepares native
SG8 operands during gather and fused gate/up, retaining BF16 activation
boundaries and using mlx-node's packed weight and sidecar layout. Splash
selects its register expert path on Apple9; its use on newer architectures
here is an independently measured experiment.

The heterogeneous projection dispatch in
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_mixed_projection.cpp and
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/mixed_projection/ adapts the fused-segment plan in
Splash's runtime/ops/LinearGguf.cpp and
runtime/metal/kernels/shared/gguf_linear.metal at the same revision. It
reuses the K-quant tile below, retaining each projection's quantization
format, K split count and separate output.

The single-sequence adaptive verification policy in
crates/mlx-core/src/models/qwen3_5_moe/verify_budget.rs and the GPU confidence
and row-budget kernels in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/dflash2_{greedy_path_confidence,verify_budget}.metal.inc
follow Splash's runtime/model/VerifyBudget.{hpp,cpp},
runtime/ops/DraftSelector.cpp and runtime/metal/kernels/decode/sampling.metal
at the same revision. The integration keeps a fixed verification shape,
skips routed-expert work beyond the selected prefix and limits acceptance
to rows whose target state was verified.

The optional FP32 selector-edge kernel in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/dflash2_selector_edges.metal.inc follows
draft_select_edges in the same sampling.metal source, with existing native
candidate arrays as inputs and every anchor predecessor row initialized.

The optional D128 draft attention kernel and host bridge in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/dflash2_attention/ and
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_dflash2_attention.cpp adapt the four-split tensor-op
attention, FP32 online softmax and fixed-order reduction in Splash's
runtime/metal/kernels/decode/draft.metal at the same revision. Live MLX
views and an explicit sliding mask replace the source ring addressing;
dynamic tensor slices bound partial tiles to initialized input rows.

The optional 256-thread target-attention reduction in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/segmented_sdpa/sdpa_segmented_nax.metal adapts
splash_attention_combine_splits from the same revision's
runtime/metal/kernels/common/paged_attention_tile.h. It supports native BF16
partials and optional FP32 partials, bounding the shared weights for up to
1024 splits. The optional FP32 denominator, page-aligned partitions,
512-key split policy and flattened dispatch follow
runtime/ops/PagedAttention.{hpp,cpp} and paged_attention_tile.h. Arbitrary
split counts require the bounded reducer; the original reducer retains its
alignment requirements. The optional Q6 head FP32 output policy follows
Splash's vocabulary projection while retaining native input and weight
staging arithmetic.

The optional producer-prepared SG8 operands in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/{gdn_fused_step,attention_sg8_prepare}.metal.inc
and their host bridges follow the fused out-projection input preparation in
runtime/metal/kernels/decode/{gdn,attention_qkv}.metal and
runtime/metal/kernels/common/gguf_sgmatrix.h. They retain mlx-node's native
BF16 arithmetic, packing and sum order. The optional SG8 split-K kernels in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/kquant/kquant.h and their launch policy in
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_kquant_register_plan.h follow
runtime/metal/kernels/decode/linear_gguf_sgmatrix.metal and
runtime/ops/LinearGguf.cpp, with 32-column tiles and whole 256-input
superblocks. Both native split kernel families share the source's
publication and last-arrival reduction protocol through
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/kquant/kquant_split_reduce.h.

The optional exact H2048 RMS kernels in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/source_norm.metal.inc and their host bridge
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_source_norm.cpp adapt the same revision's
runtime/metal/kernels/common/rms_inverse.h,
runtime/metal/kernels/shared/normalization.metal and
runtime/ops/Normalization.cpp. They preserve the source's ordered
256-thread reduction, optional 1024-thread staged schedule, FP32 norm
weights and BF16 input, residual-add and output boundaries.

The optional exact-width Q4 mixer projection in
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_source_mixer.cpp and
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/source_mixer.metal.inc adapts
runtime/metal/kernels/decode/linear_gguf_sgmatrix.metal and
runtime/metal/kernels/common/{gguf_sgmatrix,sgmatrix,split_reduce}.h at
that revision. It preserves source Table16 packing, 64-column tiles,
eight whole-superblock K splits, ordered FP32 partial reduction and the
single BF16 residual epilogue. Native T64 payloads are read through an
exact integer chunk permutation; weights are not numerically converted.
The measured-device diagnostic is separate from native SG8 operands.

The optional measured-companion convolution bridge in
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_source_draft_conv.cpp and
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/source_draft_conv.metal.inc adapts
runtime/metal/kernels/decode/draft.metal::draft_conv_phase at that
revision. It preserves the two current-row dynamic taps, ordered FP32
products and sum, and the finish residual before a single BF16 store.
The source arithmetic is isolated from the native BF16 operation policy.

The optional strict Q6 vocabulary head in
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_source_head_q6.cpp and
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/source_head_q6.metal.inc adapts
runtime/metal/kernels/common/{gguf_staged,gguf_staged_tile,quant_formats}.h
and runtime/metal/kernels/shared/gguf_linear.metal at that revision.
It preserves signed-half decoding, the spread K walk, device-A MPP input,
per-SIMDgroup stage barriers and FP32 output. Only native T64 code and
metadata addressing is adapted; generic projections remain separate.

The M = 8 K-quant tensor-op kernel in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/kquant/kquant_m8_nax.h (compiled into
paged_attn.metallib by crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/kquant/kquant_m8_nax.metal)
and its host-side K split rule in crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_kquant_metal.cpp
(qmm_m8_nax_splits) are ported from Splash's
runtime/metal/kernels/common/gguf_staged.h,
runtime/metal/kernels/common/gguf_staged_tile.h,
runtime/metal/kernels/common/split_reduce.h,
runtime/metal/kernels/shared/gguf_linear.metal (the staged decode tile) and
runtime/ops/LinearGguf.cpp (decodeSplits), with the per-format dequantization
rewritten for mlx-node's weight layout; its Q2_K decode (Codes<Q2K>,
bytes8<Q2K> and the CoefCursor Q2K arm) and the QuantKind notion of
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/kquant/kquant_mode.h (KQ_LINEAR / KQ_CODEBOOK /
KQ_INT8 / KQ_GRID) follow Splash's FmtQ2K, quant_spread2 and QuantKind in
runtime/metal/kernels/common/quant_formats.h. The IQ1_S / IQ1_M / IQ2_XXS /
IQ2_XS / IQ2_S / IQ3_XXS / IQ3_S grid decode in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/kquant/kquant_grid.h (and its C++ twin in
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_kquant.cpp) — the 7-bit sign index expansion
(kq_signs7), the per-chunk grid index / sign / scale extraction (IQ3_S's
two 9th index bits per chunk and per-element sign bits), the IQ1
"code - 9" delta form and the power-of-two scale shift — follows Splash's
FmtIQ2XXS, FmtIQ2XS, FmtIQ2S, FmtIQ3XXS, FmtIQ3S, FmtIQ1S, FmtIQ1M,
quant_signs7, quant_iq1_codes and the QuantGrid arm of dequant32 in
runtime/metal/kernels/common/quant_formats.h and
runtime/metal/kernels/common/gguf_staged.h, with the byte fetch rewritten for
mlx-node's three-array layout. The tensor-op verify attention kernel
in crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/segmented_sdpa/sdpa_segmented_nax.metal follows
the matmul2d operand shapes and the page softmax of Splash's
runtime/metal/kernels/common/paged_attention_tile.h, with the segmented
(prefix / new) K/V addressing, causal limits and partial-tile handling
written for mlx-node's two-pass layout. The DFlash2 commit structure — the
packed per-layer GDN state blobs with current/next parity
(crates/mlx-core/src/models/qwen3_5/gdn_blob.rs), the all-layer GDN commit
kernel with the conv carry folded in
(crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/gdn_commit.metal.inc,
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_gdn_commit.cpp) and the one-dispatch KV row store
(crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/kv_store_rows.metal.inc,
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_kv_store.cpp) — follows Splash's
runtime/metal/kernels/decode/gdn.metal (verify_gdn_commit, gdn_conv_carry),
runtime/ops/GDN.cpp, runtime/ops/StateLayout.hpp and
runtime/metal/kernels/common/paged_store_row.h, with the arithmetic kept
as mlx-node's per-token bf16 replay and the flat (non-paged) cache layout.
The fused GDN step (crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/gdn_fused_step.metal.inc,
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_gdn_fused.cpp) — one threadgroup per value head
running the window's recurrence, then the gated RMSNorm and z gate on the
rows kept in threadgroup memory, writing the window-final state into the
next-parity blob so a full accept is a parity swap (gdn_commit_phase's
early return) — follows the structure of Splash's verify_gdn_fused
(gdn_decode_scan, gdn_decode_gate) in runtime/metal/kernels/decode/gdn.metal
and runtime/ops/GDN.cpp, with the arithmetic kept as MLX's rms_norm kernel
and compiled sigmoid gate so the result equals mlx-node's unfused chain.

The optional source-routing path in
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/source_routing.metal.inc and its dedicated
Fast-math JIT encoder in mlx_splash_moe.cpp adapt the FP32 router matrix
projection, top-k selection, normalization and fused shared scalar gate from
runtime/metal/kernels/shared/gguf_float.metal, shared/moe.metal,
common/sgmatrix.h and common/activation.h at the same Splash revision. The
native BF16 router weights are widened exactly; this diagnostic uses the
source FP32 arithmetic and retains a separate, explicitly selected policy.

The opt-in original Q/K RMS normalization and RoPE primitive in
crates/mlx-sys/src/mlx_source_qk_norm_rope.cpp and
crates/mlx-sys/src/metal/common/source_qk_norm_rope.metal.inc adapts
Splash common/attention_qkv_prepare.h, common/rms_inverse.h and
common/target_rope.h at the revision above. It preserves the source
256-thread reduction, BF16 normalization boundary and FP32 rotary
arithmetic while accepting separately owned strided MLX inputs.

